+## Current activation (momentum cost-sensitivity on the collected universe — 44492888569 / R-001)
+
+Campaign slot 2, task R-001. Question: does the qualified short-horizon
+momentum edge survive conservative transaction-cost stress on the collected
+real-data universe?
+
+Method (predeclared before execution):
+
+- Universe: the existing 10-asset collected adjusted-close universe (dataset
+  `yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03`); manifest 10/10 OK; preflight PASSED;
+  leakage PASS on AMZN/JPM.
+- Signal: `momentum_signals` (long the previous N-day return, hold 1 day, daily
+  rebalance), lookbacks 3/5/10.
+- Walk-forward per segment: train=252d/test=84d/warmup=60d/overlap=60d; 4
+  contiguous volatility blocks; min 400 bars/segment; matched coin-flip null
+  (`noise_benchmark`) on the same segments and under the same cost configuration.
+- Cost grid: {0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0} x the repository's existing realistic cost
+  model (commission_per_trade=2.0, commission_per_share=0.003,
+  slippage_cents=2.0, slippage_proportional=0.0005); 2.0x is the conservative
+  stress.
+- Classification (predeclared): `edge(m)` = `stress_segments` verdict
+  REGIME_STABLE and all segment medians > 0; COST_ROBUST = edge(1.0) and
+  edge(2.0); COST_RESILIENT_BASE_ONLY = edge(1.0) and not edge(2.0);
+  COST_FRAGILE = edge(0.0) and not edge(1.0); NO_PRE_COST_EDGE = not edge(0.0).
+- A-priori prediction (declared before execution): COST_ROBUST <= 3/10 at
+  lookback 5 (and <= 3/10 at lookbacks 3 and 10); >= 6/10 COST_ROBUST at any
+  lookback falsifies it.
+
+Results:
+
+- Lookback 3: COST_ROBUST=6 (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA),
+  NO_PRE_COST_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM).
+- Lookback 5: COST_ROBUST=5 (AAPL, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA), COST_FRAGILE=1
+  (MSFT), NO_PRE_COST_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM).
+- Lookback 10: COST_ROBUST=5 (MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA),
+  NO_PRE_COST_EDGE=5 (AAPL, NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM).
+- Overall 16/30 COST_ROBUST, 13 NO_PRE_COST_EDGE, 1 COST_FRAGILE. The
+  a-priori prediction is falsified: 5/10 COST_ROBUST at lookback 5, not <= 3/10.
+- Lookback 5 at 1.0x: median candidate +0.069, median matched null -0.008.
+
+Independent verification: all gates MATCH. Gate 1 fresh `walk_forward` +
+`noise_benchmark` recomputation of AMZN/JPM at every lookback and cost
+multiplier; Gate 2 the zero-cost column matches
+`momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json` on all 10 tickers x 3 lookbacks
+(segments, medians, null medians, verdicts); Gate 3 the classification and
+break-even multiplier reproduce 30/30; determinism identical; 168/168
+regression tests pass.
+
+Critical cost-model limitation (durable negative/methodological finding): the
+existing engine adds slippage to the fill price on both buys and sells
+(`research/backtest/engine.py:154-167`), so slippage is a gain on sells and the
+cost model is not a conservative stress for daily-rebalanced long-biased
+signals. Candidate medians are essentially invariant to the cost multiplier:
+AAPL lookback 5 +0.070 at 0.0x and 2.0x; MSFT +0.062/+0.062; AMZN
++0.076/+0.076; TSLA +0.107/+0.107; NVDA +0.013/+0.011. The matched null is also
+unstable at positive costs for NVDA: bankruptcy-scale fold returns (e.g.
+-27.631 at 0.5x lookback 10) and large positive median nulls after clipping
+(0.396 at 1.0x lookback 5); null-dispersion changes flip framework verdicts
+(MSFT lookback 5 REGIME_STABLE at 0.5x -> REGIME_DEPENDENT at 1.0x while
+candidate medians remain [0.052, 0.072]). The COST_ROBUST classification is
+therefore conditional on the existing cost model, not evidence that the
+momentum edge survives a valid conservative cost stress.
+
+Assessment: cost robustness is UNVERIFIED. The activation produced a
+reproducible, independently verified classification and a verified methodology
+defect: the existing cost model must be repaired (symmetric slippage charged on
+both sides; commission/position sizing bounded so the matched null cannot go
+bankrupt) before the cost-robustness question can be answered. The
+frontier-first selection was correct: it targeted the decision-relevant
+qualification, falsified the a-priori prediction, and exposed a blocker that
+would otherwise invalidate future cost claims. Next: repair the cost model and
+rerun this check and verifier.
+
+---
+
